              in the diagram are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+sequences"} homotopy fiber sequences
              in the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory+of+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} homotopy theory of super L-∞ algebras
            %p
              By the discussion at
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+WZW+terms#ConsecutiveWZWTermsAndTwists"} geometry of physics – WZW terms – Consecutive WZW terms
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#FSS13"} FSS 13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
              to this yields two consecutive higher WZW terms of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi conn
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mover
                                %mover
                                  %mi ℝ
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                                %mo ˜
                              %mrow
                                %mn 10
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mn 32
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                    %mi L
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi M
                                    %mn 5
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 5
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 2
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi conn
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 10
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mn 32
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                    %mi L
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi M
                                    %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi conn
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbf{B}^{2}(\mathbb{R}/\Gamma_1)_{conn} &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \widetilde {\hat{\mathbb{R}}}^{10,1\vert \mathbf{32}}
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\mathbf{L}_{M5}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}^{5} (\mathbb{R}/\Gamma_2)_{conn}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \mathbb{R}^{10,1\vert \mathbf{32}}
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\mathbf{L}_{M2}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}^2 (\mathbb{R}/\Gamma_1)_{conn}
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              (Here by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/van+Est+isomorphism"} van Est isomorphism
              we do not notationally distinguish
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
              regarded as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
              or a
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+group"} super Lie group
            %p
              By example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#11dSugreEquationsOfMotionFromDefiniteGlobalization"}
              a choice of definite globalization of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_{M2}
              is equivalent to bosonic solution
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\mathbf{g})
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+equations"} Einstein equations
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
              equipped with a compatible globally defined WZW term
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mn 2
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_{M2}^X
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma+model"} Green-Schwarz sigma model
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExtendedSpacetimeIsConsistent"}
              this defines an extended superspacetime
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde{\hat X}
              which is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Cartan+geometry"} higher Cartan geometry
              of locally modeled on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+3-algebra"} supergravity Lie 3-algebra
              on which the local
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma+model"} Green-Schwarz sigma model
              is defined, and hence may ask for a choice of definite globalization of that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mover
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                              %mo ˜
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msubsup
                                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                    %mi L
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi M
                                    %mn 5
                                  %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 5
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 2
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi conn
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msubsup
                                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                    %mi L
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi M
                                    %mn 2
                                  %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi conn
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\widetilde {\hat{X}}
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\mathbf{L}^X_{M5}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}^{5} (\mathbb{R}/\Gamma_2)_{conn}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    X
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\mathbf{L}^X_{M2}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}^2 (\mathbb{R}/\Gamma_1)_{conn}
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is now a globally well defined background for the M5-brane sigma model and def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BPSGroupForConsecutiveWZWTerms"}
              determines its BPS-char super-6-group. By corollary
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KSExtensionForHeis"}
              this is a super 6-group extension of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superisometry+group"} superisometry group
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\mathbf{g})
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mn 5
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi FlatConn
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mover
                        %mover
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo ˜
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{B}^5 (\mathbb{R}/\Gamma_2))\mathbf{FlatConn}(\widetilde{\hat X})
            %p
              By the discussion at
              %em
                %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+WZW+terms#ConsecutiveWZWTermsAndTwists"} geometry of physics – WZW terms – Consecutive WZW terms
              the extended spacetime
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde {\hat X}
              here is such that smooth maps into it
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Sigma \longrightarrow \widetilde{\hat X}
            %p
              (which are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma+model"} sigma model
              with WZW term
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi L
                        %mrow
                          %mi M
                          %mn 5
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}^X_{M5}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a smooth function
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon \Sigma \longrightarrow X
                  into the actual spacetime
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∇
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
                  in
                  = succeed "-twisted" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ϕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+cohomology"} Deligne cohomology
                  on
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Σ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} 2-form gauge field
                  on
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Σ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ϕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            %p
              The first item here is the evident
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma+model"} sigma model
              field, the second 2-form field is part of the “tensor multiplet” on the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
              %em higher
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauged+WZW+model"} gauged WZW model
            %p
              Now to consider the BPS charge group of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi L
                        %mrow
                          %mi M
                          %mn 5
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}^X_{M5}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BPSGroupForConsecutiveWZWTerms"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KSExtensionForHeis"}
              this is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group+extension"} ∞-group extension
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-isometry+group"} super-isometry group
              of the 11-dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+spacetime"} super spacetime
              by the moduli stack
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 5
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi FlatConn
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{B}^5 U(1))\mathbf{FlatConn}(\widetilde{\hat X})
              of flat 5-form connection on the extended spacetime.
            %p
              This receives a map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 5
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi FlatConn
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 5
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi FlatConn
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{B}^5 U(1))\mathbf{FlatConn}(\hat X) \longrightarrow (\mathbf{B}^5 U(1))\mathbf{FlatConn}(\widetilde{\hat X})
              from the moduli of 5-form connections of the extended spacetime
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X
              (which is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mover
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo ˜
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde{\hat X}
              %em differential
              cohomologica data in
              = succeed "):" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi L
                        %mrow
                          %mi M
                          %mn 2
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_{M2}^X
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^2 (\mathbb{R}/\Gamma_1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
              which sits in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+sequence"} homotopy fiber sequence
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi DD
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msubsup
                                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                    %mi L
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi M
                                    %mn 2
                                  %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbf{B}^2 (\mathbb{R}/\Gamma_1)
                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    \\hat X
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; X &amp;\stackrel{\mathbf{DD}(\mathbf{L}_{M2}^X)}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}^3 (\mathbb{R}/\Gamma_1)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+differentiation"} Lie differentiation
              as in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#0TruncationOfHigherPoissonBracket"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 5
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi FlatConn
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{B}^5 U(1))\mathbf{FlatConn}(\widetilde{\hat X})
              turns into
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 5
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi FlatConn
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{B}^5 \mathbb{R})\mathbf{FlatConn}(\widetilde{\hat X})
              hence into
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ♭
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mn 5
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}(\hat X, \flat \mathbf{B}^5 \mathbb{R})
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∫
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ♭
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X
              = succeed "-fibration" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+space"} K(Z,3)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∫
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo →
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int \hat X \to \int X
              over the underlying bare
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
              of spacetime
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              which is classified by the integral degree-4 class which is the higher
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dixmier-Douady+class"} Dixmier-Douady class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi DD
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mn 5
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} DD(\mathbf{L}_{M5}^X)
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi L
                        %mrow
                          %mi M
                          %mn 2
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_{M2}^{X}
            %p
              The degree-5 real cohomology of such a fibration is computed by a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+spectral+sequence"} Serre spectral sequence
              %em
                %a{:href => "Eilenberg-Mac+Lane+space#CohomologyOfEMSpaces"} Eilenberg-MacLane space – cohomology of EM spaces
              only very few entries in this spectral sequence contribute, and the result is the middle cohomology of this sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mn 4
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 5
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mn 4
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 6
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^1(X) \stackrel{(0,d_4)}{\longrightarrow} H^2(X) \oplus H^5(X)
                    \\stackrel{(d_4,0)}{\longrightarrow}
                    H^6(X)
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn 4
                    %mo ∝
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi DD
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mn 2
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_4 \propto (-)\cup DD(\mathbf{L}_{M2}^X)
              is given by taking the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cup+product"} cup product
              with the class of the M2-WZW term.
            %p
              This is the group of M2-brane and M5-brane charges with corrections by global effects, in the corrected
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+super+Lie+algebra"} M-theory super Lie algebra
              for the superspacetime
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,g)
